>How the hell did you manage to get a +20 weapon without it disintegrating ?

Probably the same way I had a +49 Mjollnir once (you haven't lived until
you've creamed a major demon in two blows...).  Save file abuse.

Really el-cheapo way to win the game follows...






This shouldn't be any secret, but it probably hasn't occured to some
people out there.  When you save a game, Nethack deposits a save file on
your system.  When you resume, it deletes the file.  But, all you have
to do is make a copy of the save file and call it something different. 
If something undesireable happens, you just rename your backup save file
to what nethack called your old save file, and you're set.  Do this
repeatedly and you can do just about anything.  For example, you could
keep dipping stuff in a fountain until a water demon gave you a wish. 
Or, you could always get a glowing potion and keep opening it until a
genie gave you a wish.  Or, you could see how high you could enchant
your weapon and get a +49 Mjollnir.  This isn't even a bug in the
game...it's just cheap.

